{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 16628591283794977877, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 622, "mtime": 1791871734.184191, "sha256": "7222b712d3891ac15b9c87c01daa36540fe7ece067433a80548e8f5356c11446"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 357, "mtime": 1791871736.7643974, "sha256": "5d8734664ae0a8ec9a0b7533b5861ff7ae43d46b25b8e5fc64680c05830a7693"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/7/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/7/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Add a regression test, then run.\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\nThere were two causes in `round(x, 2)`:\n- The float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so it rounds down.\n- Python's built-in `round()` rounds halves to the nearest even digit, not up. For example, `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now turns the float into a `Decimal` using `repr(x)`, the shortest decimal that gives back the same float (`'2.675'`). It then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and still returns a `float`, so callers get the same type as before. `add_vat` uses this function, so it gets the fix too.\n\nNegative halves round away from zero (`-2.675` \u2192 `-2.68`), which is the usual rule for money.\n\n**Test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, which checks `2.675`\u2192`2.68`, `0.125`\u2192`0.13`, `2.674`\u2192`2.67` and `-2.675`\u2192`-2.68`. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the test functions directly with `python3`: the new test and the existing `test_split` both pass. I also spot-checked `add_vat`: `add_vat(10)` = `12.0`, `add_vat(1.99)` = `2.39`, `add_vat(2.2291666)` = `2.67`. The last one is right because the true value is `2.67499992`.\n\n**Possible separate bug in `split`:** it uses `int(total * 100)`, which cuts off decimals instead of rounding. Inputs like `0.29` come out as `28.999\u2026` cents, so they likely split wrong. I didn't test or change this, since it wasn't part of the request.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 251109, "requests_cache_write": 10964, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1521018, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2349, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_